{{define "doctrine"}}{{template "head" .}}
{{$d := .Data}}
<div class="topbar"><h1>How Counterfoil decides</h1>
  <span class="crumb">the rules of the house, read from this instance's own configuration — not a brochure</span></div>
<main id="main">
<div class="stack">

  <div class="card">
    <div class="hd"><h2>The one idea</h2></div>
    <div class="bd" style="max-width:72ch">
      <p style="margin-top:0"><b>A reply is a claim; the record is the fact.</b> Every HR action on
      another team's system runs under a warrant — who asked, under which rule and, for reserved
      decisions, a named person's signed approval of exactly that request — and a step counts as
      done only when the target system's own record confirms it. Every state change leaves a
      counterfoil: a hash-chained, countersigned receipt an auditor can re-check offline.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:0">An agent's message cannot close anything. A success reply cannot.
      A timeout cannot. The kill switch cannot — pausing agents never extends a legal deadline.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row">
    <div class="card" style="flex:1;min-width:0">
      <div class="hd"><h2>The evidence ladder</h2><span class="note">what a verdict is allowed to rest on</span></div>
      <div class="bd">
        <table class="t">
          <tr><th style="width:120px">Level</th><th>Meaning</th><th style="width:190px">What it may close</th></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="ev ev-attributed">attributed</span></td>
            <td>the target's own record carries <b>our</b> reference — proof our request did this</td>
            <td>anything, money clocks included</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="ev ev-observed">observed</span></td>
            <td>the end state is right, but cannot be tied to our request</td>
            <td>convergent state changes (disable, revoke)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="ev ev-reply_only">reply_only</span></td>
            <td>only the target's reply claims success — nothing to read back</td>
            <td class="note">never a money clock; declared and justified per effect</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="ev ev-internal">internal</span></td>
            <td>the fact lives in our own ledger (a decision, a computation)</td>
            <td>internal steps</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="flex:1;min-width:0">
      <div class="hd"><h2>The warrant path</h2><span class="note">every external effect, in order</span></div>
      <div class="bd">
        <ol class="warrantpath">
          <li>Policy gate — reserved list, kill switch, mandate hash check</li>
          <li>Intent ledger — PENDING, synced to disk before any bytes leave</li>
          <li>Send once — with <span class="mono">Idempotency-Key</span> and <span class="mono">X-Client-Ref</span></li>
          <li>Read back the target's own record, by our reference</li>
          <li>Done at its evidence level — or IN DOUBT, to a named person</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="note">A crash between send and commit is reconciled on restart by reading the
        target, never by resending blindly. A changed request after approval — one rupee added —
        fails the mandate's hash check and is refused, with a receipt.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card tight">
    <div class="hd"><h2>Reserved decisions</h2>
      <span class="note">{{len $d.Reserved}} on this instance — the floor can be added to, never removed</span></div>
    <table class="t">
      <tr><th style="width:80px">ID</th><th>Decision</th><th style="width:150px">Guarded action</th>
        <th style="width:120px">Approver role</th><th style="width:90px"></th></tr>
      {{range $d.Reserved}}
      <tr><td><b>{{.ID}}</b></td><td>{{.Title}}</td>
        <td>{{if .Action}}<span class="mono" style="font-size:11.5px">{{.Action}}</span>{{else}}<span class="note">decision-only</span>{{end}}</td>
        <td>{{.ApproverRole}}{{if .RouteOnly}} <span class="note">· route only</span>{{end}}</td>
        <td>{{if .Floor}}<span class="pill p-reserved">floor</span>{{else}}<span class="pill p-pending">added</span>{{end}}</td></tr>
      {{end}}
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="row">
    <div class="card tight" style="flex:1.2;min-width:0">
      <div class="hd"><h2>The rule pack</h2>
        <span class="note">v{{$d.Rules.Version}} · dated {{$d.Rules.Dated}} · demo fixtures, flagged where legal confirmation is needed</span></div>
      <table class="t">
        <tr><th>Rule</th><th>As configured</th><th>Citation</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Notice period</td><td>{{$d.Rules.Notice.Days}} days{{if $d.Rules.Notice.BuyoutAllowed}}, buyout allowed{{end}}</td>
          <td class="note">{{$d.Rules.Notice.Cite}}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Final wages</td><td>within {{$d.Rules.FinalWages.WorkingDays}} working days of the last working day
            {{if $d.Rules.FinalWages.NeedsLegalConfirmation}}<span class="legal">needs_legal_confirmation</span>{{end}}</td>
          <td class="note">{{$d.Rules.FinalWages.Cite}}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Gratuity</td><td>from {{printf "%.2f" $d.Rules.Gratuity.MinYears}} years' service, due in {{$d.Rules.Gratuity.DueDays}} days
            {{if $d.Rules.Gratuity.NeedsLegalConfirmation}}<span class="legal">needs_legal_confirmation</span>{{end}}</td>
          <td class="note">{{$d.Rules.Gratuity.Cite}}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Relieving letter</td><td>within {{$d.Rules.RelievingLetter.Days}} days</td>
          <td class="note">{{$d.Rules.RelievingLetter.Cite}}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Leave encashment</td><td>unused earned leave, gross/30 per day</td>
          <td class="note">{{$d.Rules.LeaveEncashment.Cite}}</td></tr>
      </table>
      <div class="bd note">Working-day arithmetic skips weekends and the sample holiday calendar:
        {{range $i, $h := $d.Holidays}}{{if $i}} · {{end}}{{$h}}{{end}}.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="flex:1;min-width:0">
      <div class="hd"><h2>What the admission check refuses</h2>
        <span class="note">a service line activates only as data, only past these</span></div>
      <div class="bd">
        <ul class="refuselist">
          <li>An approval decided by silence or by timeout — forbidden outright</li>
          <li>A reserved effect that does not sit under its approval step</li>
          <li>An external effect with no read-back declaration and no justification</li>
          <li>An approval that could complete without a named person</li>
          <li>Dependency cycles between steps</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="note">A package that passes gets a certificate hash; <b>two named people</b>
        activate exactly that hash. The onboarding package ships inactive so activation can be
        shown live, in the controls room.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
</main>
{{template "foot" .}}{{end}}
